      "silencesAtLeast1_5s": [],
      "lowScoreWords": [],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "You've seen this separation before, so here it is in fast forward. Add water, and the salt dissolves while the sand doesn't. Pour it through filter paper, and the sand stays behind as the residue, while the salty liquid, the filtrate, runs through. Rinse the sand with a little water to wash off any salt, then dry it. The filtrate goes into an evaporating basin, and we heat it gently until most of the water has gone, then leave it somewhere warm to finish drying. Now each component sits in its own container.",
